  "question": {
    "text": "Nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is having mass number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn></math> and its binding energy per nucleon is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>. It splits in two fragments <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>105</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>115</mn></math>. The binding energy of nucleons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math> per nucleon. The energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> released per fission will be:",
    "image": null
  },
